Theorem TF-6: Apply (with contract) transfer = refine(CONSERVATIVE, contract)

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Apply { dst, func, args }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-6
    - `func` has `MemoryContract` available — callee analyzed; contract
      includes a `ReturnContract` (IC-4) with `uniqueness`, `locality`,
      `shape` narrowing fields available to refine TF-5's CONSERVATIVE
    - `refine(base, contract)` per Annex E §AIMS TF-6 inline definition:
      result.uniqueness := contract.uniqueness
      result.locality := contract.locality
      result.shape := contract.shape
      // Access, Consumption, Cardinality, Effect preserved from base
    - Per Appendix A row 7: `dst := (Owned, Unrestricted, Many,
      contract.uniq, contract.loc, contract.shape, ALL)`

  Soundness property:
    Forall contract in ReturnContract.
      transfer_tf6(Apply { _ }, contract) =
        Tagged::State {
          access = Owned; // preserved from CONSERVATIVE
          consumption = Unrestricted; // preserved from CONSERVATIVE
          cardinality = Many; // preserved from CONSERVATIVE
          uniqueness = contract.uniqueness; // narrowed by refine()
          locality = contract.locality; // narrowed by refine()
          shape = contract.shape; // narrowed by refine()
          effect = ALL = 0b111; // preserved from CONSERVATIVE
        }
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: for fixed contract c, refine(_, c) is a
    constant function on its first argument (TF-6 always passes
    CONSERVATIVE); trivially monotone per L-4 reflexivity.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Refine narrowing enumeration — for representative contracts,
          verify the 3 narrowed dimensions (Uniqueness x Locality x Shape)
          take the contract's values; the 4 preserved dimensions
          (Access x Consumption x Cardinality x Effect) stay at
          CONSERVATIVE.
      (b) Per-row Appendix A correctness — Appendix A row 7 enumerates
          exactly the 7 dimensions above; verify per-column emission.
      (c) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — refine(CONSERVATIVE, c) is constant
          in the first argument (always CONSERVATIVE); trivially monotone.

    Part (a) — refine narrowing on representative ReturnContracts (5 contracts
    sampled to span the (Uniqueness x Locality x Shape) product carrier):
      contract_1 = { uniqueness: Unique, locality: BlockLocal,
                     shape: ReusableStruct }
        — Tightest narrowing path: fresh allocation returns; enables
          downstream RL-22 KnownSafe + RL-29 noalias.
      contract_2 = { uniqueness: Unique, locality: FunctionLocal,
                     shape: CollectionBuffer }
        — Fresh collection return; supplies precise locality and shape to
          backend-neutral fact freezing and representation projection.
      contract_3 = { uniqueness: MaybeShared, locality: Unknown,
                     shape: NonReusable }
        — Conservative-equivalent contract (degenerate refine no-op).
      contract_4 = { uniqueness: Shared, locality: HeapEscaping,
                     shape: NonReusable }
        — Pessimistic contract: callee explicitly returns shared heap.
      contract_5 = { uniqueness: Unique, locality: ArgEscaping,
                     shape: ReusableEnum }
        — ArgEscaping unique return; rare but valid (callee returns
          fresh allocation that escapes through caller's argument).

      For each contract, verify TF-6 output:
        access = Owned (preserved); consumption = Unrestricted (preserved);
        cardinality = Many (preserved); effect = ALL = 0b111 (preserved);
        uniqueness = contract.uniqueness (narrowed);
        locality = contract.locality (narrowed);
        shape = contract.shape (narrowed).

    Part (b) — Appendix A row 7 column verification:
      Row 7 = (Owned, Unrestricted, Many, contract.uniq, contract.loc,
               contract.shape, ALL).
      Per-column emission matches refine output: 4 preserved-from-
      CONSERVATIVE columns + 3 narrowed-by-contract columns. Verified
      column-by-column for each of the 5 sample contracts.
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-6 explicit guidance:
        "Dimensions NOT narrowed by refine: Access (stays Owned — call
        results always owned by caller), Consumption (stays Unrestricted —
        caller may use result arbitrarily), Cardinality (stays Many —
        refined by actual usage during backward demand), Effect (stays ALL
        — EffectSummary governs this, not ReturnContract)."

    Part (c) — constant-function monotonicity:
      TF-6 always passes CONSERVATIVE as the first argument to refine:
        transfer_tf6(contract) = refine(CONSERVATIVE, contract).
      For fixed contract c, refine(CONSERVATIVE, c) is constant — first
      argument always CONSERVATIVE; output depends solely on c.
      Per L-4 reflexivity: refine(CONSERVATIVE, c) ≤ refine(CONSERVATIVE, c).
      Hence the function f(_) = refine(CONSERVATIVE, c) is monotone for
      any state input — same input always produces same output for given
      contract.

      Stronger monotonicity claim (not required by L-6 but verified by the
      refinement engine): refine is monotone in its first argument for
      fixed contract. If a ≤ b in the product order, then refine(a, c) ≤
      refine(b, c) — the 4 preserved dimensions inherit ≤ from (a, b);
      the 3 narrowed dimensions become equal (= c.uniq, c.loc, c.shape)
      hence reflexively comparable. This stronger property is dispatched
      to the refinement engine as PRIMARY discharge.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) per-rule discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf6_apply_contract_refine — constant-in-first-arg
        check for refine(CONSERVATIVE, c))
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 5-contract sample enumeration covering the
        (Uniqueness x Locality x Shape) carrier per
        section_04::verify_tf6_apply_contract_refine)
      refinement (PRIMARY — refine() narrowing-correctness check:
        Uniqueness x Locality x Shape narrowed from CONSERVATIVE; Access x
        Consumption x Cardinality x Effect preserved at CONSERVATIVE per
        Annex E §AIMS TF-6 + section_04::verify_tf6_apply_contract_refine)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; product order at §02)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis + refinement engines discharge TF-6 via 5-contract enumeration + per-column refine() narrowing-correctness check + constant-in-first-arg monotonicity
